### Journey C — Failed corporate payment

1. Billing obligation becomes due.
2. Payment collection is attempted.
3. Payment fails or remains pending.
4. Payment status is synchronized.
5. Merchant identifies the affected account and obligation.
6. Merchant applies the agreed recovery and credit policy.
7. Customer is notified.
8. Successful recovery is reconciled to the original obligation.

A failed payment does not automatically suspend a corporate service. Service suspension remains subject to merchant policy and system integration.

