### Experience principles

- Identify the corporate account clearly.
- Display the correct contract or service reference.
- Distinguish each billing obligation.
- Show amount due and billing period.
- Make payment references easy to copy and reconcile.
- Provide clear payment status.
- Avoid exposing one department's information to another without authorization.
- Support corporate finance and procurement approval workflows through the merchant's systems.

## 10. Payment management and reconciliation

### Payment scenarios

| Scenario | Recommended handling |
|---|---|
| One bill paid successfully | Update the matching obligation |
| Multiple bills paid separately | Reconcile each obligation |
| Partial payment | Validate allocation and remaining-balance handling |
| Duplicate payment | Detect and resolve before financial posting |
| Payment pending | Avoid duplicate collection |
| Wrong reference | Investigate and reconcile manually |
| Overdue payment | Apply merchant collection policy |
| Payment from another payer | Validate payer authorization and reference mapping |

### Important distinction

Payment collection and financial allocation are different activities.

For example, a corporate customer may transfer one amount intended to settle several service obligations. The merchant must define how that payment is allocated.

Do not assume FlexiBill automatically performs cross-obligation allocation or consolidated settlement.

### Recommended reconciliation fields

- Corporate Customer ID.
- Account ID.
- Contract ID.
- Billing ID.
- Billing period.
- Amount due.
- Amount paid.
- Payment status.
- Transaction ID.
- Payment timestamp.
- Reconciliation status.

## 11. Failure and exception management

| Scenario | Business risk | Recommended control |
|---|---|---|
| Customer account mismatch | Wrong account settlement | Reference validation |
| Duplicate billing | Overcollection | Idempotency and billing controls |
| Duplicate payment event | Incorrect financial posting | Event deduplication |
| Failed payment | Overdue receivable | Recovery workflow |
| Contract changed | Incorrect amount | Merchant-side contract recalculation |
| Service terminated | Future billing continues | Stop or adjust billing |
| Account closed | Unresolved obligations | Closure and reconciliation process |
| Branch reassignment | Incorrect allocation | Merchant master-data update |
| Partial settlement | Incorrect outstanding balance | Merchant allocation rules |
| Unmatched payment | Reconciliation backlog | Exception queue |

